      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Types of Weathering"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Weathering is an in-situ (static) process involving the disintegration and decomposition of rocks.",
        "Mechanical weathering causes physical breakdown of rocks without altering their mineral composition.",
        "Chemical weathering decomposes rock minerals through chemical reactions, forming new compounds.",
        "Special weathering forms include biological weathering, spheroidal weathering, and block disintegration.",
        "Weathering rates depend heavily on climatic conditions, rock composition, structural features, and vegetation cover."
      ],
      "id": "m5exo0n"
    },
